WEBVTT


00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:34.104
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.716
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:41.547
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:41.721 --> 00:00:45.452
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:49.425
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:49.595 --> 00:00:53.190
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:53.366 --> 00:00:56.927
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:57.103 --> 00:01:00.630
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:01:00.807 --> 00:01:04.174
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:07.609
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.477
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:15.678
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:15.855 --> 00:01:19.450
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.753
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:26.695
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:29.858
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:33.528
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:33.706 --> 00:01:36.971
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:37.143 --> 00:01:39.168
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:43.446
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:48.514
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:48.688 --> 00:01:51.987
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:52.158 --> 00:01:54.092
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:32.756
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:34.092
You have an appointment...


00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.861
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:37.036 --> 00:02:39.971
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:40.139 --> 00:02:42.198
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:43.899
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:44.343 --> 00:02:46.174
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:46.345 --> 00:02:48.176
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:48.614 --> 00:02:49.740
Bath. Now.


00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:52.581
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:53.953 --> 00:02:55.181
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:58.758 --> 00:03:00.851
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:03:01.027 --> 00:03:03.621
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:03:03.796 --> 00:03:06.230
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:19.712 --> 00:03:21.145
Victor, no.


00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.754
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:29.922 --> 00:03:35.918
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:36.395 --> 00:03:38.920
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:39.632 --> 00:03:41.327
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:42.835 --> 00:03:44.427
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:44.971 --> 00:03:46.336
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:47.507 --> 00:03:49.134
Nothing.


00:03:53.779 --> 00:03:56.646
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:56.816 --> 00:03:58.181
Just run them over if you have to.


00:04:00.987 --> 00:04:04.013
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:07.421
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:07.593 --> 00:04:11.051
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.324
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.161
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:16.335 --> 00:04:18.530
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:18.704 --> 00:04:22.162
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:26.107
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:26.279 --> 00:04:28.975
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:29.148 --> 00:04:32.242
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:32.418 --> 00:04:33.908
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:34.086 --> 00:04:36.646
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:36.822 --> 00:04:38.619
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:52.171 --> 00:04:56.130
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:56.309 --> 00:04:59.676
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:59.845 --> 00:05:01.710
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:05:01.881 --> 00:05:04.315
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:05:04.483 --> 00:05:08.010
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:08.187 --> 00:05:11.748
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:12.258 --> 00:05:17.161
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.161
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:19.665 --> 00:05:23.658
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:27.139 --> 00:05:29.471
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:29.942 --> 00:05:35.005
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:35.314 --> 00:05:38.442
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:38.618 --> 00:05:41.678
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:43.356 --> 00:05:45.620
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:45.791 --> 00:05:49.227
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.724
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:53.899 --> 00:05:55.730
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:57.003 --> 00:06:00.200
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:06:00.373 --> 00:06:04.139
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.971
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:07.146 --> 00:06:08.909
That record was amazing.


00:06:09.081 --> 00:06:12.050
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:13.552 --> 00:06:16.020
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:16.188 --> 00:06:19.089
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:19.258 --> 00:06:20.919
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:22.461 --> 00:06:28.024
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.361
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:30.536 --> 00:06:33.903
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:34.073 --> 00:06:36.234
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:36.409 --> 00:06:38.775
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:38.944 --> 00:06:42.846
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:43.983 --> 00:06:46.076
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:46.585 --> 00:06:48.951
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:49.522 --> 00:06:51.649
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:51.824 --> 00:06:53.792
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:53.959 --> 00:06:55.950
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:56.128 --> 00:06:59.097
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:59.532 --> 00:07:02.296
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:07:02.468 --> 00:07:05.369
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:07:05.538 --> 00:07:07.369
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.407
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:10.576 --> 00:07:13.204
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.670
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:15.848 --> 00:07:17.440
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:17.616 --> 00:07:19.982
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:20.152 --> 00:07:23.553
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:24.156 --> 00:07:29.560
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:38.437 --> 00:07:40.132
Watch out.


00:07:40.606 --> 00:07:42.631
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:43.642 --> 00:07:47.237
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:47.413 --> 00:07:49.210
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:49.381 --> 00:07:51.747
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:53.282
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:53.452 --> 00:07:56.444
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:56.622 --> 00:08:00.581
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.489
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:08:03.329 --> 00:08:05.229
You giving our ball back or what?


00:08:05.397 --> 00:08:09.026
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:13.839 --> 00:08:17.104
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:19.445 --> 00:08:23.176
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:23.349 --> 00:08:24.714
Hotter.


00:08:24.884 --> 00:08:26.511
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:26.685 --> 00:08:28.915
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:29.088 --> 00:08:31.648
First time for everything, right?


00:08:38.798 --> 00:08:40.493
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:40.666 --> 00:08:41.894
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:42.368 --> 00:08:45.428
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:45.604 --> 00:08:47.799
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:47.973 --> 00:08:51.431
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.874
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:54.046 --> 00:08:57.413
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:57.683 --> 00:09:00.015
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:09:00.186 --> 00:09:01.710
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:09:01.887 --> 00:09:04.788
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:09:04.957 --> 00:09:08.393
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:08.561 --> 00:09:12.088
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:12.264 --> 00:09:17.429
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:17.603 --> 00:09:21.164
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:23.433
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:23.609 --> 00:09:26.510
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:26.679 --> 00:09:28.806
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:28.981 --> 00:09:32.007
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:32.184 --> 00:09:34.379
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:42.928 --> 00:09:44.190
Whoa.


00:09:44.363 --> 00:09:47.457
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:47.633 --> 00:09:50.295
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:50.469 --> 00:09:51.629
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:51.804 --> 00:09:55.205
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:55.374 --> 00:09:57.035
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:57.209 --> 00:09:58.233
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.878
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:10:01.046 --> 00:10:03.446
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:10:03.616 --> 00:10:05.516
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:10:05.684 --> 00:10:07.311
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:07.887 --> 00:10:09.980
Om.


00:10:10.789 --> 00:10:13.417
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:13.592 --> 00:10:15.685
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:15.861 --> 00:10:18.386
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:18.764 --> 00:10:20.391
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:21.901 --> 00:10:23.061
My butt is numb.


00:10:23.402 --> 00:10:26.599
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:26.772 --> 00:10:30.230
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:30.409 --> 00:10:33.503
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:33.679 --> 00:10:35.670
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:36.749 --> 00:10:42.585
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:42.755 --> 00:10:46.316
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:47.192 --> 00:10:50.252
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:50.429 --> 00:10:53.023
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:53.198 --> 00:10:54.495
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:57.192
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:57.369 --> 00:11:00.566
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:11:00.739 --> 00:11:03.173
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:11:03.342 --> 00:11:06.743
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:10.516 --> 00:11:11.983
Victor.


00:11:12.151 --> 00:11:17.384
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:41.046 --> 00:11:45.483
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:45.818 --> 00:11:48.309
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:49.355 --> 00:11:52.017
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:52.191 --> 00:11:56.753
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:12:00.065 --> 00:12:01.089
<i>Ow.</i>


00:12:01.266 --> 00:12:03.700
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:12:03.869 --> 00:12:05.461
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:12:05.671 --> 00:12:07.901
Mac and cheese.


00:12:08.807 --> 00:12:11.935
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:12.478 --> 00:12:14.036
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:19.551 --> 00:12:22.918
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:23.088 --> 00:12:26.421
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:27.826 --> 00:12:31.023
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:31.196 --> 00:12:33.289
How did this become my life?


00:12:33.465 --> 00:12:36.457
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:36.635 --> 00:12:38.125
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:38.303 --> 00:12:39.736
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:40.172 --> 00:12:42.367
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:42.541 --> 00:12:44.873
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:47.713 --> 00:12:50.580
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:52.351 --> 00:12:53.648
Now look at me.


00:12:53.819 --> 00:12:56.310
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:56.488 --> 00:12:59.480
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:59.658 --> 00:13:01.649
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:13:01.827 --> 00:13:04.057
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:04.229 --> 00:13:05.992
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:07.533 --> 00:13:09.728
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:09.902 --> 00:13:12.393
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:12.805 --> 00:13:16.036
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:16.208 --> 00:13:19.974
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:20.145 --> 00:13:23.774
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:24.716 --> 00:13:27.116
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:27.286 --> 00:13:29.880
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:30.055 --> 00:13:32.922
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:33.092 --> 00:13:34.116
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:34.293 --> 00:13:36.853
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:37.029 --> 00:13:38.963
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:39.131 --> 00:13:42.157
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:42.334 --> 00:13:44.359
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:44.536 --> 00:13:46.504
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:46.672 --> 00:13:47.696
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:47.873 --> 00:13:51.741
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.311
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:55.481 --> 00:13:58.575
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.048
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:03.154
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:03.322 --> 00:14:05.552
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:05.724 --> 00:14:08.921
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:09.094 --> 00:14:13.360
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:13.532 --> 00:14:15.500
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:16.001 --> 00:14:19.528
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:22.074 --> 00:14:27.512
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:27.679 --> 00:14:30.239
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:30.415 --> 00:14:32.508
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:32.684 --> 00:14:34.413
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:34.586 --> 00:14:37.214
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:37.389 --> 00:14:40.722
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:40.893 --> 00:14:42.520
Again.


00:14:42.694 --> 00:14:44.252
Really? Okay.


00:14:44.429 --> 00:14:50.061
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:50.235 --> 00:14:51.361
Ouch.


00:14:51.537 --> 00:14:54.597
I could belch the song better.


00:14:56.208 --> 00:14:58.369
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:58.544 --> 00:15:00.011
Anything to forget I live here.


00:15:00.179 --> 00:15:03.080
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:03.248 --> 00:15:07.150
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:07.519 --> 00:15:11.182
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:15.394 --> 00:15:17.760
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.659
No.


00:15:19.831 --> 00:15:22.129
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:34.313 --> 00:15:37.612
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:37.783 --> 00:15:40.251
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:50.729 --> 00:15:53.823
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:58.704 --> 00:16:00.433
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:16:00.606 --> 00:16:01.698
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:16:01.873 --> 00:16:05.969
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:06.144 --> 00:16:07.475
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:07.646 --> 00:16:10.410
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:10.849 --> 00:16:12.146
Victor!


00:16:12.317 --> 00:16:15.548
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:15.721 --> 00:16:17.882
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:21.393 --> 00:16:23.020
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:32.938 --> 00:16:34.098
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:34.273 --> 00:16:35.672
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:35.841 --> 00:16:39.277
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:39.444 --> 00:16:41.105
Crap.


00:16:44.516 --> 00:16:46.211
This is insane.


00:16:46.385 --> 00:16:50.446
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:17:00.232 --> 00:17:02.325
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:04.069 --> 00:17:05.696
Crap.


00:17:09.007 --> 00:17:12.602
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:12.778 --> 00:17:16.578
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:16.748 --> 00:17:18.875
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:19.051 --> 00:17:20.746
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:20.919 --> 00:17:23.479
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:23.655 --> 00:17:26.715
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:26.892 --> 00:17:29.122
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:29.294 --> 00:17:31.421
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:33.765 --> 00:17:35.232
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:41.406 --> 00:17:43.271
Victor.


00:17:47.112 --> 00:17:48.545
Katie?


00:17:49.748 --> 00:17:51.978
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:52.184 --> 00:17:55.449
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:58.384
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:59.424 --> 00:18:01.255
The truth. Um...


00:18:02.561 --> 00:18:05.894
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:06.064 --> 00:18:07.395
Naked.


00:18:08.433 --> 00:18:10.731
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:10.902 --> 00:18:12.426
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:14.873 --> 00:18:15.965
There.


00:18:16.141 --> 00:18:19.338
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:23.949 --> 00:18:25.576
I'm kidding.


00:18:26.118 --> 00:18:27.949
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:28.286 --> 00:18:29.310
No, no.


00:18:29.488 --> 00:18:32.889
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:33.058 --> 00:18:35.253
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:35.861 --> 00:18:40.525
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:41.032 --> 00:18:44.832
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:45.003 --> 00:18:47.597
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:51.476 --> 00:18:53.137
What is that?


00:18:53.712 --> 00:18:55.976
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:56.148 --> 00:18:58.116
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:59.317 --> 00:19:01.046
Hey. What...?


00:19:13.899 --> 00:19:16.390
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:16.568 --> 00:19:18.195
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.497
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:20.672 --> 00:19:22.936
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:23.108 --> 00:19:24.132
Do you hear this?


00:19:24.309 --> 00:19:25.970
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:26.144 --> 00:19:27.839
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:28.013 --> 00:19:30.345
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:30.515 --> 00:19:32.710
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:32.884 --> 00:19:34.749
She gave you a CD?


00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:38.287
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:39.524 --> 00:19:43.392
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:44.629 --> 00:19:48.725
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:50.702 --> 00:19:52.897
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:54.039 --> 00:19:55.597
So...


00:19:56.475 --> 00:19:58.602
...that meeting today...


00:19:58.777 --> 00:20:01.575
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:20:01.913 --> 00:20:03.972
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:04.149 --> 00:20:06.583
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:06.852 --> 00:20:08.046
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:09.521 --> 00:20:11.421
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:14.718
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:14.993 --> 00:20:18.724
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:23.635 --> 00:20:26.433
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:26.605 --> 00:20:29.665
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:29.841 --> 00:20:32.105
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:36.081 --> 00:20:37.742
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:39.417 --> 00:20:40.714
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:40.886 --> 00:20:43.980
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:44.155 --> 00:20:46.623
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:46.791 --> 00:20:48.952
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:49.127 --> 00:20:50.321
That's interesting.


00:20:50.495 --> 00:20:53.259
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:53.431 --> 00:20:54.659
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:54.833 --> 00:20:56.460
I only have cheese.


00:20:59.638 --> 00:21:01.606
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:21:01.773 --> 00:21:03.673
Your phone.


00:21:06.711 --> 00:21:09.578
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:09.748 --> 00:21:11.306
I have underestimated you.


00:21:11.883 --> 00:21:13.714
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:13.885 --> 00:21:16.979
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:17.155 --> 00:21:19.783
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:19.958 --> 00:21:24.156
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:24.329 --> 00:21:27.594
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:27.766 --> 00:21:31.202
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:31.369 --> 00:21:34.497
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:34.673 --> 00:21:39.804
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:41.079 --> 00:21:43.240
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:48.653 --> 00:21:53.283
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:53.458 --> 00:21:57.554
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:57.729 --> 00:22:01.495
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:22:01.967 --> 00:22:03.628
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:03.802 --> 00:22:05.963
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:09.207 --> 00:22:11.903
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:12.477 --> 00:22:15.935
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:16.381 --> 00:22:18.349
I like trouble.


00:22:19.884 --> 00:22:21.010
Hey, kids.


00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.756
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:25.924 --> 00:22:28.688
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:32.694
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:32.998 --> 00:22:38.231
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:38.436 --> 00:22:40.904
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:41.172 --> 00:22:43.732
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:43.908 --> 00:22:45.876
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:46.044 --> 00:22:49.104
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:52.340
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:52.517 --> 00:22:55.213
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:55.387 --> 00:22:58.686
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:58.857 --> 00:23:00.688
What if I don't want to?


00:23:01.793 --> 00:23:05.524
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:05.697 --> 00:23:07.756
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:07.932 --> 00:23:10.196
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:10.368 --> 00:23:13.929
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:14.105 --> 00:23:15.595
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:15.774 --> 00:23:17.241
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:18.843 --> 00:23:20.970
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:21.146 --> 00:23:24.274
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:24.683 --> 00:23:28.881
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:29.054 --> 00:23:32.888
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:33.058 --> 00:23:35.959
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:36.127 --> 00:23:38.391
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:38.563 --> 00:23:40.690
You are a star.


00:23:40.865 --> 00:23:45.063
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:45.236 --> 00:23:46.794
I'm a star.


00:23:46.971 --> 00:23:51.135
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:51.309 --> 00:23:53.709
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:53.878 --> 00:23:55.846
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:56.014 --> 00:23:57.572
Every part of him.


00:23:57.749 --> 00:24:01.276
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:24:01.453 --> 00:24:04.217
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:08.050
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:08.226 --> 00:24:10.126
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:10.729 --> 00:24:12.629
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:12.797 --> 00:24:15.493
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:15.667 --> 00:24:17.726
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:17.902 --> 00:24:19.267
Are we clear?


00:24:19.704 --> 00:24:20.898
Crystal.


00:24:22.841 --> 00:24:25.833
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:30.003
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:30.181 --> 00:24:32.649
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:32.817 --> 00:24:34.148
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:34.319 --> 00:24:36.446
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:36.621 --> 00:24:38.145
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:38.323 --> 00:24:41.690
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:41.860 --> 00:24:44.556
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:44.729 --> 00:24:46.993
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:47.165 --> 00:24:48.723
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:51.027
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:51.202 --> 00:24:52.669
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:52.837 --> 00:24:55.670
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:58.502
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:58.676 --> 00:25:00.439
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:25:00.612 --> 00:25:02.307
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:02.747 --> 00:25:05.443
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:05.617 --> 00:25:08.347
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:09.714
We're here to impress.


00:25:09.888 --> 00:25:12.152
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:15.994 --> 00:25:18.462
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:18.630 --> 00:25:20.894
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:21.065 --> 00:25:23.260
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:23.434 --> 00:25:26.801
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:26.971 --> 00:25:29.496
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:29.674 --> 00:25:32.939
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:33.111 --> 00:25:38.413
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:38.583 --> 00:25:45.318
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:46.524 --> 00:25:48.014
That's good.


00:25:55.066 --> 00:25:58.365
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:59.204 --> 00:26:01.536
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:26:01.706 --> 00:26:03.606
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:04.642 --> 00:26:08.237
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:08.413 --> 00:26:10.608
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:10.782 --> 00:26:12.716
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:12.884 --> 00:26:18.117
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:18.289 --> 00:26:20.484
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:21.025 --> 00:26:22.788
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:22.961 --> 00:26:25.555
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:26.164 --> 00:26:29.463
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:29.634 --> 00:26:31.101
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:31.269 --> 00:26:33.294
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:33.471 --> 00:26:36.463
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:38.643 --> 00:26:41.077
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:44.616 --> 00:26:46.447
Okay.


00:26:47.018 --> 00:26:49.384
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:49.721 --> 00:26:51.484
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:51.656 --> 00:26:53.647
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:53.825 --> 00:26:55.656
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:55.827 --> 00:26:58.125
That I shall not cross.


00:26:58.596 --> 00:27:00.894
So sing something.


00:27:02.567 --> 00:27:04.034
Okay.


00:27:08.172 --> 00:27:10.970
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:11.142 --> 00:27:13.633
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:13.811 --> 00:27:15.210
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:15.680 --> 00:27:17.671
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:19.484 --> 00:27:21.952
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:22.120 --> 00:27:24.645
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:24.822 --> 00:27:26.414
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:26.925 --> 00:27:28.552
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:32.495
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:32.664 --> 00:27:34.996
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:35.166 --> 00:27:36.633
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:38.036 --> 00:27:39.697
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:40.638 --> 00:27:43.471
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:43.641 --> 00:27:48.840
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:49.013 --> 00:27:50.571
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:51.683 --> 00:27:54.277
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:54.452 --> 00:27:57.012
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:57.188 --> 00:28:01.557
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:02.961 --> 00:28:05.623
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:05.797 --> 00:28:08.061
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:08.232 --> 00:28:10.894
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:11.069 --> 00:28:13.560
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:18.042 --> 00:28:20.169
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:20.345 --> 00:28:22.973
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:23.147 --> 00:28:26.480
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:26.751 --> 00:28:29.242
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:29.420 --> 00:28:31.411
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:31.589 --> 00:28:33.887
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:34.058 --> 00:28:35.753
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:36.027 --> 00:28:37.722
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:38.162 --> 00:28:41.996
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:42.467 --> 00:28:46.563
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:46.738 --> 00:28:47.762
...good acoustics.


00:28:48.172 --> 00:28:52.006
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:52.176 --> 00:28:53.768
If you gave them your song.


00:28:55.179 --> 00:28:56.840
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:57.582 --> 00:29:00.278
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:29:00.451 --> 00:29:01.782
Yeah.


00:29:03.454 --> 00:29:09.984
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:10.294 --> 00:29:11.591
You wrote that song today?


00:29:11.763 --> 00:29:15.221
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:15.500 --> 00:29:16.797
You really like this guy.


00:29:16.968 --> 00:29:18.663
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:18.836 --> 00:29:21.031
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:21.205 --> 00:29:24.697
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:26.511 --> 00:29:29.309
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:32.917 --> 00:29:35.750
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:37.789 --> 00:29:40.257
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:40.591 --> 00:29:44.083
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:44.262 --> 00:29:46.287
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:46.464 --> 00:29:47.488
Am not.


00:29:48.533 --> 00:29:51.525
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:51.702 --> 00:29:54.398
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:54.572 --> 00:29:57.132
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:57.308 --> 00:30:00.004
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:30:00.178 --> 00:30:02.112
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:06.307
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:06.684 --> 00:30:09.778
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:12.723 --> 00:30:14.247
Okay.


00:30:14.559 --> 00:30:16.151
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:16.327 --> 00:30:17.658
That's my girl.


00:30:17.929 --> 00:30:21.922
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:22.100 --> 00:30:25.399
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:25.570 --> 00:30:27.333
What? Why?


00:30:27.505 --> 00:30:28.870
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:32.777 --> 00:30:34.335
Katie!


00:30:34.512 --> 00:30:37.948
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:38.116 --> 00:30:39.606
Go.


00:30:39.784 --> 00:30:41.513
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:41.686 --> 00:30:43.017
Angie, heads up.


00:30:44.989 --> 00:30:46.286
Katie!


00:30:51.496 --> 00:30:53.225
What's going on?


00:30:53.397 --> 00:30:54.830
Nothing.


00:30:54.999 --> 00:30:58.127
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:58.302 --> 00:31:00.600
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:31:00.771 --> 00:31:04.832
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:08.079 --> 00:31:12.243
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:12.416 --> 00:31:14.646
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:14.819 --> 00:31:16.252
Oh, no, no.


00:31:16.420 --> 00:31:18.911
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:19.090 --> 00:31:21.388
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:21.559 --> 00:31:24.255
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:24.428 --> 00:31:25.452
Fun.


00:31:25.630 --> 00:31:28.758
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:28.933 --> 00:31:32.334
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:33.204 --> 00:31:35.229
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:39.210 --> 00:31:41.576
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:41.913 --> 00:31:44.177
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:44.482 --> 00:31:47.576
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:47.852 --> 00:31:51.015
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:51.355 --> 00:31:54.415
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:54.592 --> 00:31:56.992
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:57.161 --> 00:32:00.096
So let's just get this party started.


00:32:00.264 --> 00:32:04.291
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:04.569 --> 00:32:07.868
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:09.073 --> 00:32:10.370
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:20.351 --> 00:32:22.615
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:22.787 --> 00:32:24.982
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:25.590 --> 00:32:28.616
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:29.794 --> 00:32:32.922
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:33.698 --> 00:32:35.962
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:36.133 --> 00:32:38.431
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:38.603 --> 00:32:41.800
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:45.009 --> 00:32:47.637
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:47.812 --> 00:32:50.872
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:51.048 --> 00:32:54.245
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:55.152 --> 00:32:58.019
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:58.189 --> 00:33:00.248
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:33:00.424 --> 00:33:01.516
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:02.126 --> 00:33:04.617
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:04.795 --> 00:33:06.262
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:06.998 --> 00:33:08.329
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:08.499 --> 00:33:09.523
Mm-hm.


00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:11.099
Right.


00:33:12.103 --> 00:33:13.502
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:16.574 --> 00:33:17.836
Hmm.


00:33:22.647 --> 00:33:24.638
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:25.316 --> 00:33:26.340
Ravi?


00:33:28.019 --> 00:33:30.544
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:30.721 --> 00:33:33.155
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:35.293 --> 00:33:37.853
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:38.029 --> 00:33:39.223
Obviously.


00:33:39.764 --> 00:33:42.255
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:42.433 --> 00:33:43.991
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:44.168 --> 00:33:47.535
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:48.072 --> 00:33:51.200
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:51.375 --> 00:33:54.037
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:54.412 --> 00:33:57.813
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:57.982 --> 00:33:59.847
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:34:00.217 --> 00:34:01.741
But I never got my shot.


00:34:01.919 --> 00:34:04.149
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:04.322 --> 00:34:06.722
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:06.891 --> 00:34:09.086
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:09.260 --> 00:34:10.750
"Who is asking?"


00:34:11.028 --> 00:34:14.395
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:14.565 --> 00:34:17.159
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:17.335 --> 00:34:21.704
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:22.006 --> 00:34:24.270
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:24.442 --> 00:34:26.842
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:27.178 --> 00:34:29.806
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:29.980 --> 00:34:31.174
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:32.383 --> 00:34:35.079
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:37.888 --> 00:34:41.551
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:42.226 --> 00:34:44.285
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:44.462 --> 00:34:46.930
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:47.098 --> 00:34:48.156
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:49.734 --> 00:34:51.065
Blow it up.


00:34:53.003 --> 00:34:54.561
Thank you.


00:35:04.382 --> 00:35:05.781
Whoa.


00:35:05.950 --> 00:35:08.578
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:08.753 --> 00:35:11.813
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:13.190 --> 00:35:15.522
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:15.693 --> 00:35:18.924
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:21.632 --> 00:35:24.601
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:24.769 --> 00:35:28.398
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:29.106 --> 00:35:31.438
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:36.814 --> 00:35:38.247
Where is he?


00:35:39.083 --> 00:35:41.881
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:42.052 --> 00:35:43.713
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:43.888 --> 00:35:46.322
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:49.827 --> 00:35:53.388
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:53.564 --> 00:35:56.897
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:57.067 --> 00:35:59.262
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:59.470 --> 00:36:02.200
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:02.373 --> 00:36:04.807
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:11.615 --> 00:36:12.673
I think I found him.


00:36:12.850 --> 00:36:15.114
Well, he is blond.


00:36:18.222 --> 00:36:20.520
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:22.426 --> 00:36:24.724
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:24.895 --> 00:36:26.294
What are you doing here?


00:36:26.464 --> 00:36:29.297
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:29.467 --> 00:36:31.492
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:31.669 --> 00:36:34.604
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:34.772 --> 00:36:36.603
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:36.774 --> 00:36:39.242
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:41.679 --> 00:36:43.806
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:45.349 --> 00:36:48.785
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:48.953 --> 00:36:51.148
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:51.322 --> 00:36:54.189
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:54.358 --> 00:36:56.292
...and you're fired.


00:36:59.330 --> 00:37:02.857
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:05.469 --> 00:37:06.959
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:07.204 --> 00:37:08.330
You were amazing.


00:37:08.506 --> 00:37:09.564
Do I know you?


00:37:13.911 --> 00:37:16.505
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:18.849 --> 00:37:20.908
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:21.552 --> 00:37:24.043
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:28.559 --> 00:37:31.392
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:31.562 --> 00:37:32.927
Miss Van R.


00:37:33.564 --> 00:37:35.964
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:36.133 --> 00:37:37.327
...but were never good enough?


00:37:38.702 --> 00:37:40.363
Who told you that?


00:37:58.088 --> 00:37:59.521
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:59.690 --> 00:38:02.887
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:03.060 --> 00:38:04.186
Oh!


00:38:04.361 --> 00:38:08.593
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:12.937 --> 00:38:16.031
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:16.206 --> 00:38:19.107
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:23.881 --> 00:38:26.611
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:26.951 --> 00:38:29.647
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:29.820 --> 00:38:31.082
Follow me.


00:38:36.126 --> 00:38:37.957
Oh, wow.


00:38:40.431 --> 00:38:45.994
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:46.870 --> 00:38:48.770
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:48.939 --> 00:38:52.636
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:54.144 --> 00:38:55.338
Or not.


00:38:57.615 --> 00:39:00.641
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:06.857 --> 00:39:10.418
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:11.729 --> 00:39:15.961
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:16.133 --> 00:39:19.660
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:19.837 --> 00:39:23.830
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:25.809 --> 00:39:29.142
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:30.914 --> 00:39:34.611
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:35.285 --> 00:39:38.982
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:39.456 --> 00:39:42.289
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:42.760 --> 00:39:43.852
Uh-uh.


00:42:22.786 --> 00:42:25.380
I think I've blown something.


00:42:25.556 --> 00:42:28.616
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:31.228 --> 00:42:32.786
Move it, fatso.


00:42:34.531 --> 00:42:41.130
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:41.872 --> 00:42:45.501
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:58.055 --> 00:42:59.488
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:59.656 --> 00:43:01.681
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:43:01.859 --> 00:43:04.419
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:04.595 --> 00:43:06.563
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:09.032 --> 00:43:10.397
I'm so sorry.


00:43:11.101 --> 00:43:12.329
What...? You...?


00:43:13.036 --> 00:43:14.697
Hey. Wait.


00:43:14.872 --> 00:43:16.100
But who are you?


00:43:16.273 --> 00:43:18.867
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:27.017 --> 00:43:30.043
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:48.505 --> 00:43:50.530
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:51.308 --> 00:43:54.243
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:54.678 --> 00:43:57.613
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:57.948 --> 00:44:00.143
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:02.152 --> 00:44:05.315
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:05.489 --> 00:44:09.050
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:09.226 --> 00:44:11.490
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:11.662 --> 00:44:14.722
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:15.032 --> 00:44:18.160
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:19.069 --> 00:44:22.197
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:28.712 --> 00:44:31.943
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:32.115 --> 00:44:34.174
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:34.351 --> 00:44:36.285
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:36.453 --> 00:44:38.148
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:38.322 --> 00:44:40.620
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:41.992 --> 00:44:46.122
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:47.097 --> 00:44:50.692
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:51.768 --> 00:44:53.395
We're recording.


00:44:53.704 --> 00:44:55.535
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:55.706 --> 00:44:56.934
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:57.541 --> 00:44:59.475
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:59.643 --> 00:45:01.372
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:45:01.545 --> 00:45:03.877
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:04.047 --> 00:45:05.275
Check this out, all right?


00:45:05.449 --> 00:45:09.044
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:09.219 --> 00:45:11.050
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:11.221 --> 00:45:13.052
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:13.256 --> 00:45:15.281
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:15.459 --> 00:45:16.619
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:16.793 --> 00:45:18.761
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:18.929 --> 00:45:20.794
That was subpar at best.


00:45:20.964 --> 00:45:23.489
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:24.234 --> 00:45:27.533
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:27.704 --> 00:45:29.262
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:29.439 --> 00:45:31.805
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:31.975 --> 00:45:35.001
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:35.178 --> 00:45:38.272
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:38.448 --> 00:45:40.006
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:40.450 --> 00:45:43.317
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:43.854 --> 00:45:47.415
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:47.691 --> 00:45:51.024
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:51.194 --> 00:45:53.788
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:53.964 --> 00:45:56.432
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:56.600 --> 00:45:59.694
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:59.870 --> 00:46:02.395
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:04.141 --> 00:46:08.737
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:08.912 --> 00:46:11.881
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:12.049 --> 00:46:14.882
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:20.924 --> 00:46:24.121
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:43.246 --> 00:46:45.544
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:45.715 --> 00:46:46.909
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:47.084 --> 00:46:49.382
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:49.553 --> 00:46:50.918
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:51.755 --> 00:46:53.882
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:54.057 --> 00:46:55.183
This is not good.


00:46:56.760 --> 00:46:58.557
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:58.728 --> 00:47:00.559
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:47:00.730 --> 00:47:03.130
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:03.300 --> 00:47:06.736
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:06.903 --> 00:47:07.927
Listen...


00:47:08.105 --> 00:47:11.541
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:11.708 --> 00:47:13.369
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:25.222 --> 00:47:29.215
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:29.392 --> 00:47:32.384
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:32.562 --> 00:47:36.191
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:36.366 --> 00:47:40.302
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:40.470 --> 00:47:44.270
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:44.808 --> 00:47:47.709
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:47.878 --> 00:47:50.938
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:52.749 --> 00:47:54.683
It was you?


00:47:55.352 --> 00:47:58.446
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:59.389 --> 00:48:03.223
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:04.861 --> 00:48:07.887
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:08.064 --> 00:48:10.828
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:11.001 --> 00:48:13.128
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:13.770 --> 00:48:16.500
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:16.773 --> 00:48:18.536
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:18.708 --> 00:48:22.075
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:22.245 --> 00:48:24.509
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:26.016 --> 00:48:27.813
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:27.984 --> 00:48:29.076
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:30.020 --> 00:48:31.487
You have a date with detention.


00:48:31.655 --> 00:48:33.122
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:33.290 --> 00:48:35.019
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:35.192 --> 00:48:37.888
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:38.061 --> 00:48:41.189
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:41.364 --> 00:48:42.854
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:43.033 --> 00:48:44.933
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:45.101 --> 00:48:47.899
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:48.071 --> 00:48:50.437
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:50.607 --> 00:48:52.074
Fine.


00:48:52.876 --> 00:48:54.400
I hate you.


00:48:58.048 --> 00:49:02.178
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:02.452 --> 00:49:04.386
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:10.961 --> 00:49:12.588
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:12.762 --> 00:49:15.959
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:16.132 --> 00:49:17.599
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:17.767 --> 00:49:20.565
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:20.737 --> 00:49:22.932
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


